Text:
  This mathematical companion separates exact list operations, numerical error
  bounds, IEEE arithmetic, and program correctness. The first two layers are
  implemented in the accompanying modules. The IEEE and C layers remain pending.

-- Required interface: valid format(p,e); Float(p,e); value; finite;
-- floating add, floating multiply, floating fma, floating zero.
-- These must come from a verified IEEE model, not unconstrained parameters.
-- The intended rounding mode and admissible precision/exponents must be pinned.

Define real vector(x):
  Let p,e: Natural
  Let x: List(Float(p,e))
  Returns: List(Real)
  Equals: map(function(a: Float(p,e),value(a)),x)

Define real matrix(A):
  Let p,e: Natural
  Let A: List(List(Float(p,e)))
  Returns: List(List(Real))
  Equals: map(function(row: List(Float(p,e)),real vector(row)),A)

Define computed dot(x,y):
  Let p,e: Natural
  Let x,y: List(Float(p,e))
  Returns: Float(p,e)
  Equals: dot(floating add(p,e),floating multiply(p,e),floating zero(p,e),x,y)

Define computed fused dot(x,y):
  Let p,e: Natural
  Let x,y: List(Float(p,e))
  Returns: Float(p,e)
  Equals: fused dot(floating fma(p,e),floating zero(p,e),x,y)

Define computed sum(x):
  Let p,e: Natural
  Let x: List(Float(p,e))
  Returns: Float(p,e)
  Equals: vector sum(floating add(p,e),floating zero(p,e),x)

Define computed matrix vector(A,x):
  Let p,e: Natural
  Let A: List(List(Float(p,e)))
  Let x: List(Float(p,e))
  Returns: List(Float(p,e))
  Equals: matrix vector(floating add(p,e),floating multiply(p,e),floating zero(p,e),A,x)

Text:
  The conditions dot accuracy, sum accuracy and matrix vector accuracy are
  defined in Bounds.clean. Their existential perturbations, length constraints
  and entrywise inequalities are ordinary translated Clean mathematics.
  The results below connect those conditions to concrete IEEE computations.

Result dot mixed error:
  Attribution: laproof; Theorem 1 (bfDOT); adapted
  Let p,e: Natural
  Assume format: valid format(p,e)
  Let x,y: List(Float(p,e))
  Assume dimensions: list length(x) = list length(y)
  Assume finite vector x: all entries(finite(p,e),x)
  Assume finite vector y: all entries(finite(p,e),y)
  Assume finite output: finite(p,e)(computed dot(x,y))
  Conclude:
    dot accuracy(unit roundoff(p),underflow bound(p,e),
      real vector(x),real vector(y),value(computed dot(x,y)))

Result sum backward error:
  Attribution: laproof; Theorem 2 (bSUM); adapted
  Let p,e: Natural
  Assume format: valid format(p,e)
  Let x: List(Float(p,e))
  Assume finite input: all entries(finite(p,e),x)
  Assume finite output: finite(p,e)(computed sum(x))
  Conclude: sum accuracy(unit roundoff(p),real vector(x),value(computed sum(x)))

Result matrix vector mixed error:
  Attribution: laproof; Theorem 3 (bfMV); adapted
  Let p,e: Natural
  Assume format: valid format(p,e)
  Let A: List(List(Float(p,e)))
  Let x: List(Float(p,e))
  Assume dimensions:
    all entries(function(row: List(Float(p,e)),list length(row) = list length(x)),A)
  Assume finite vector: all entries(finite(p,e),x)
  Assume finite matrix: all entries(function(row: List(Float(p,e)),all entries(finite(p,e),row)),A)
  Assume finite output: all entries(finite(p,e),computed matrix vector(A,x))
  Conclude:
    matrix vector accuracy(unit roundoff(p),underflow bound(p,e),
      real matrix(A),real vector(x),real vector(computed matrix vector(A,x)))

Result matrix vector avoids overflow:
  Attribution: laproof; Theorem 4 (finiteMV); adapted
  Let p,e: Natural
  Assume format: valid format(p,e)
  Let A: List(List(Float(p,e)))
  Let x: List(Float(p,e))
  Assume finite vector: all entries(finite(p,e),x)
  Assume finite matrix: all entries(function(row: List(Float(p,e)),all entries(finite(p,e),row)),A)
  Assume safe entries:
    safe matrix vector input(unit roundoff(p),underflow bound(p,e),e,real matrix(A),real vector(x))
  Conclude: all entries(finite(p,e),computed matrix vector(A,x))

Result fused dot mixed error:
  Attribution: laproof; Section II.A(c); adapted
  Let p,e: Natural
  Assume format: valid format(p,e)
  Let x,y: List(Float(p,e))
  Assume dimensions: list length(x) = list length(y)
  Assume finite vector x: all entries(finite(p,e),x)
  Assume finite vector y: all entries(finite(p,e),y)
  Assume finite output: finite(p,e)(computed fused dot(x,y))
  Conclude:
    dot accuracy(unit roundoff(p),underflow bound(p,e),
      real vector(x),real vector(y),value(computed fused dot(x,y)))

