Text:
  The CSR layer needs a representation with row pointers, column indices and
  values; dimension, monotonicity, index-range and row-order invariants; a pure
  fused accumulator over each row segment; and equivalence to the dense fused
  computation. The postcondition uses floating equivalence, not bitwise equality.
  The C theorem additionally needs a memory model, permission shares, separation
  assertions and preservation of the input arrays and untouched memory. None of
  those obligations is discharged by the numerical bounds or list definitions.

